---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="About | Ravikumar Buragapu"
			description="Ravikumar Buragapu is an engineering leader focused on AI engineering, agentic systems, platform engineering, and building reliable, secure, production-ready enterprise platforms."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>About</h1>

			<p>
				I'm a Director of Engineering focused on AI engineering, platform
				engineering, and reliability at enterprise scale. My work centers on
				turning emerging technologies—from GenAI to agentic systems—into
				production-ready platforms that are secure, observable, resilient,
				and built to operate at scale.
			</p>

			<p>
				I believe the next phase of AI will be defined not just by what models
				can do, but by how well we engineer the systems around them:
				identity, evaluation, permissions, infrastructure, operational
				controls, and human accountability.
			</p>

			<h2>What I work on</h2>
			<p>
				My focus spans AI infrastructure, agentic architectures, LLM
				inference, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), cloud platforms,
				site reliability engineering (SRE), and operational intelligence.
				I work at the intersection of architecture, engineering execution,
				and operations—with an emphasis on making complex systems reliable,
				secure, and measurable in production.
			</p>

			<h2>Engineering leadership and impact</h2>
			<p>
				At Oracle Health, I lead engineering across infrastructure,
				reliability, and data intelligence platforms spanning commercial,
				regulated, and Federal environments. The work involves modernizing
				critical analytics infrastructure and strengthening the operational
				foundations required for secure, highly available, data-intensive
				services.
			</p>

			<p>
				At Wells Fargo, I formed the Agentic and GenAI Squad and helped
				define the architecture and strategy for agentic workflows across
				engineering, reaching more than 10,000 developers.
			</p>

			<p>
				At Adobe, I led platform engineering, led the Agentic AI Builders
				Group, and built an AI-driven Service Maturity Insights platform.
				Earlier in my career, I held engineering roles at Kohl's and
				Charles Schwab. I began my software engineering career in India
				in 2000.
			</p>

			<h2>Technical perspective</h2>
			<p>
				I’m particularly interested in the engineering principles that
				make AI systems trustworthy and operationally sustainable:
				explicit agent identity, least-privilege access, policy-as-code,
				reproducible evaluation, observability, controlled autonomy,
				and reliable failure recovery.
			</p>

			<p>
				I also care about the broader engineering system—developer
				experience, platform abstractions, automation, and operational
				practices that help teams deliver software faster without
				compromising reliability or security.
			</p>

			<h2>Education and credentials</h2>

			<section class="education-credentials">
				<h3>Education</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>
						Ph.D. in Artificial Intelligence — University of the
						Cumberlands (In Progress)
					</li>
					<li>
						Executive MBA — Quantic School of Business and Technology
					</li>
					<li>
						Master’s in Electronics — Andhra University
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h3>Professional certifications</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>Google Cloud Professional Cloud Architect</li>
					<li>AWS Certified Solutions Architect – Professional</li>
					<li>Certified Cloud Security Professional (CCSP)</li>
					<li>ITIL Master</li>
					<li>IAPP Artificial Intelligence Governance Professional (AIGP)</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<h2>Speaking and writing</h2>
			<p>
				I have spoken at DPE Summit, Percona Community Live, and
				ScyllaDB Summit, as well as AI and machine learning panels
				in Santa Clara. My writing explores developer productivity,
				platform engineering, AI governance, and the architectural
				and operational challenges of running AI agents in production.
			</p>

			<p>
				<a href="/speak">Speaking and publications</a>
				·
				<a href="/writing">Technical writing</a>
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>